# Response headers for the static files (Workers Static Assets reads this file from dist/; it is
# not served itself). The API routes (/api, /ws, /room, /lobby, /nodes) run the Worker and are
# unaffected. Every page is served from here: index.html (/, /tv and any other path: the SPA
# fallback) and replay.html (the replay viewer, /replay.html), so this one rule covers them all.
#
# The CSP comes in two headers, both checked against the code by tests/csp.test.mjs:
#   Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: the full policy. It also gates eval and wasm compilation:
#     'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets the physics wasm compile while eval stays refused. Browsers learned that
#     keyword in Chrome 97 / Firefox 102 / Safari 16. Chromium 94 to 96 (2023 TVs: Tizen 7, webOS 23,
#     which already parse the bundle) ignore it and refuse every wasm unless eval is allowed, so
#     enforced, this policy would stop the game and the replay viewer from loading there. Report-only:
#     it reports (in the console), it refuses nothing.
#   Content-Security-Policy: enforced, the same policy without the eval gate. No default-src and no
#     script-src, which are what gates eval and wasm; script-src-elem and script-src-attr in their
#     place still refuse injected scripts, inline handlers and javascript: URLs (Chromium had both
#     well before 94, Firefox since 108, Safari before the 16.4 the bundle needs), and every other
#     directive is the full policy's.
#     When old TVs no longer matter, enforce the full policy: rename the -Report-Only header and
#     delete this one.
# The sources:
#   script-src(-elem)  the build's own modules (the music's AudioWorklet too), the sha256 of each
#                page's inline scripts (today only index.html's /tv/ redirect; the test fails when one
#                changes without its hash), Turnstile, and Cloudflare Web Analytics' beacon, which the
#                zone injects (it reports to /cdn-cgi/rum: 'self'). 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (full only).
#   style-src    'unsafe-inline': the icon sprite and the debug overlays set style attributes.
#   connect-src  the API and the match, room and lobby sockets ('self'), and the community nodes:
#                wss:// hosts on any domain.
#   media-src, manifest-src  'self', spelled out in the enforced header (default-src's value).
#   frame-src    the Turnstile challenge. frame-ancestors 'none': never in a frame (X-Frame-Options too).
# Strict-Transport-Security: HTTPS only, for a year, subdomains included (sp1 serves only HTTPS).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src-elem 'self' 'sha256-OLpvSajAB4kwvloMmj2FyovlRe1qITBh8oF1/nh19cA=' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' wss:; media-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-OLpvSajAB4kwvloMmj2FyovlRe1qITBh8oF1/nh19cA=' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' wss:; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# No long-lived Cache-Control on /assets/* although Vite content-hashes them: a request for a missing
# asset (an old tab during a deploy) gets the SPA fallback index.html, and _headers rules match the
# path, so that HTML would be cached as immutable. ETag revalidation (304) stays cheap.
